From: mscharged-port
Subject: Compile the original gameplay providers with native width contracts
Upstream-base: efa6fc84680e48bfdca7e6ac245d8abf333ae617

Temporary E13 compiler/ABI adaptations for the original match providers.
Game behavior, requests and timing are unchanged.

- Animation callback contexts: SAnim trigger callbacks (cSAnimCallback,
  CharacterTriggerHandler, CharacterAnimTriggerCallback, AnimTagScript) and
  pose-node callbacks (cPN_SAnimController playback-speed/synchronized-weight,
  cPN_SingleAxisBlender, cPN_Feather) carry owner, pool-slot and stack-record
  addresses in unsigned int words. Natively they use the existing
  PoseCallbackAddressWord (patch 0224): pointer width on hosts, unsigned int
  on console. Goalie's save-blend word keeps its original index-in-low-bits
  packing with a carrier-width mask.
- ODE: intP is pointer-sized for the obstack alignment arithmetic.
- GoalieActions' MWCC asm LobSaveOwnerDiagnostic only branches to its next
  instruction (retail code layout); natively it is an empty inline function.
- Retail emits the inline Desire::UnidentifiedVirtual7 (DesireDebug.inl) and
  UnidentifiedFuzzyVariantData constructor (FuzzyVariantCollection.inl) out of
  line in Fielder.cpp. Natively Desire.h and DesireUpdate.h include those
  unchanged inline bodies, so every referencing vtable and caller has them.
  Likewise the Desire units that call CallFielderFuzzyFunction include the
  original inline FuzzyRuntimeCall.h natively.
- PowerupBase::AwardPowerup reads the captain power-up through Wii offsets
  0x11C/0x14; natively these are cCharacter::mUnidentified11C and
  CharacterInfo::unknown_0x14.
- GoalieActions instantiates a queued-event Function<bool> through header
  inlines; natively it includes the original nlFunction.inl template bodies.
- MWCC's double __fabs(double) intrinsic maps to std::fabs on a double.
- C++ conformance MWCC accepted: `false` as the null AIContext constant, a
  jump to `default:` past case-local initializations (scoped natively), and a
  goto past an initialized local (declaration hoisted natively).
- MegaBallIndicators reads the Wii remote/freestyle DPD records at Wii byte
  offsets 0x1B0/0x1D0; natively these are WiiRemotePad::mDPDData and
  WiiFreestylePad::mDPDData, the same members feDPD.cpp names.
- WaluigiWall event owners and SHPause item contexts use the existing native
  EventOwnerHandle and pointer-width integer context casts.
- Animation trigger files (NLBT v1) are big-endian disc records: the
  BinaryTriggerFile constructor first has the checked native transport convert
  the header words and anim/trigger records of the completed load in place.
  AnimTagScript's bytecode size keeps its Wii32 pointer-word subtraction and
  its memcpy publishes the copy as completed serialized bytecode for the
  original interpreter load.
- MSL's stdlib.h inline _abs and the MWCC __declspec(section) placement of
  PhysicsGoalie's runtime-initialised constant have native equivalents; a goto
  past two PhysicsWorld locals is resolved by hoisting them natively.
- NetworkSession's pause/resume event owner cells receive the connection
  pointer from RegisterEventConnection; natively they are pointer-width, as a
  u32 is on the Wii, so the store no longer overruns the paused-machine masks
  that hold FixedUpdateTask's simulation.
- cTeam::UpdateTeamAI sorts its four fielder pointers with the Wii element
  size 4 (sizeof(cFielder*)); the native call uses the actual pointer size.

